---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
import Check from "../components/Check.astro";
import Ext from "../components/Ext.astro";
import HeroVideo from "../components/HeroVideo.astro";
import Pricing from "../components/Pricing.astro";
import ProductPreview from "../components/ProductPreview.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
// After the layout, so these rules follow the base styles in the cascade.
import "../styles/home.css";
import { APP_URL } from "../site";

const worksWith = ["GitHub.com", "Markdown and MDX", "Mermaid and other diagrams", "Keyboard and screen reader"];
---

<Base
  title="Rendered Review: review the docs in a pull request as documents"
  description="Review the Markdown and MDX in a GitHub pull request as rendered pages. Comments are saved to the pull request in GitHub. Free for public repositories."
>
  <div class="wrap hero" id="top">
    <a class="eyebrow" href="#features">Free for public repositories · open source</a>
    <h1>Review the docs in a pull request as documents</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Rendered Review opens the Markdown and MDX files in a GitHub pull request as formatted pages. Select the words you
      mean and comment on them. Every comment is saved to the pull request in GitHub, so reviewers who stay in GitHub see
      it too.
    </p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <Ext class="btn btn-primary" href={APP_URL}>Open a pull request</Ext>
      <a class="btn" href="#how">See how it works</a>
    </div>
    <p class="fine">Or put <code>renderedreview.dev/</code> in front of any pull request URL.</p>
    <HeroVideo />
    <div class="visual static-preview">
      <ProductPreview />
    </div>
    <ul class="works-with" aria-label="Compatibility">
      {
        worksWith.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <Check />
            {item}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section class="alt" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><div class="kicker">How it works</div><h2>Three steps, and GitHub stays in charge</h2><p>No new place to keep comments. Rendered Review reads the pull request from GitHub and writes your feedback back to it.</p></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Open the pull request</h3><p>Paste a pull request URL, follow the link the GitHub Action posts on the PR, or change <code>github.com/…</code> to <code>renderedreview.dev/github.com/…</code>.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Read and select</h3><p>Changed and unchanged docs render as pages, with changed sections marked. Select a phrase, sentence, table cell or diagram and write your comment.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Publish to GitHub</h3><p>Your comment is posted to the pull request in the closest form GitHub supports. The next section shows which.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="where" aria-labelledby="where-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><div class="kicker">Comments live in GitHub</div><h2 id="where-h">Where your comment ends up</h2><p>Rendered Review keeps no copy of your review. Each comment becomes a GitHub object that anyone on the pull request can read and answer.</p></div>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>
          <div><div class="case">You select text on a changed line</div><div class="snip chg"><span class="doc-path">docs/rfd/0042-webhook-retries.md</span><p>Each delay includes <span class="hl">full jitter of up to 20%</span><span class="wire" aria-hidden="true"></span> so recovering endpoints are not hit at once.</p></div></div>
          <div class="gh-card"><div class="h"><b>priya-k</b> commented on line 24<span class="kind">Review thread</span></div><div class="b"><blockquote>full jitter of up to 20%</blockquote><p>"Full jitter" usually means random in [0, delay). Which one do we mean?</p></div></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div><div class="case">You select text the PR didn't change, in a changed file</div><div class="snip"><span class="doc-path">docs/rfd/0042-webhook-retries.md</span><p>The dispatcher <span class="hl">retries failed deliveries indefinitely</span><span class="wire" aria-hidden="true"></span>, holding a worker slot for days.</p></div></div>
          <div class="gh-card"><div class="h"><b>priya-k</b> commented on the file<span class="kind">File comment</span></div><div class="b"><blockquote>retries failed deliveries indefinitely</blockquote><p>Do we know how long the longest one ran? A number here would make the case.</p></div></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div><div class="case">You comment on a document the PR didn't touch</div><div class="snip"><span class="doc-path">docs/reliability.md</span><p>Webhook consumers must respond within <span class="hl">10 seconds</span><span class="wire" aria-hidden="true"></span>.</p></div></div>
          <div class="gh-card"><div class="h"><b>jlo</b> commented<span class="kind">PR comment</span></div><div class="b"><div class="ref">docs/reliability.md · permalink @ e41f0c2</div><blockquote>10 seconds</blockquote><p>Does the new timeout change this?</p></div></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div><div class="case">You suggest a change on a changed line</div><div class="snip chg"><span class="doc-path">docs/rfd/0042-webhook-retries.md</span><p>After the <del>last</del> <ins>final</ins><span class="wire" aria-hidden="true"></span> attempt the event moves to the dead-letter queue.</p></div></div>
          <div class="gh-card"><div class="h"><b>mchen</b> suggested a change<span class="kind">GitHub suggestion</span></div><div class="b"><div class="snip-sug"><del>After the last attempt</del><ins>After the final attempt</ins></div><p>The author can apply it from GitHub with one click.</p></div></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="flow-foot">Comments made directly in GitHub show up in Rendered Review too, so it doesn't matter where each reviewer works.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" id="features">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><div class="kicker">Features</div><h2>Built for reading, not diffing</h2></div>
      <div class="features">
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4L1.5 8 5 12M11 4l3.5 4-3.5 4"/></svg></div><h3>Markdown and MDX</h3><p>GitHub Flavored Markdown, front matter and alerts. MDX components show as labelled source, and nothing in the file is run.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="1.5" y="5.5" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/><rect x="10.5" y="2" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/><rect x="10.5" y="10" width="4" height="4" rx="1"/><path d="M5.5 7.5h2.5V4h2.5M8 7.5V12h2.5"/></svg></div><h3>Diagrams, rendered</h3><p>Mermaid, Graphviz, Vega, WaveDrom, maps and STL models render in the browser. Comment on the diagram or its source.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"/><path d="M8 4.5V8l2.5 1.5"/></svg></div><h3>Comments survive revisions</h3><p>After a push, comments are matched to the new text. Uncertain matches are marked outdated, never dropped.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 3.5h11v7h-6l-3 2.5v-2.5h-2z"/></svg></div><h3>Unchanged docs too</h3><p>Switch from changed docs to all docs and comment on any Markdown file in the repository at that commit.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"/><path d="M6.5 5.5l4 2.5-4 2.5z"/></svg></div><h3>One link per pull request</h3><p>An optional GitHub Action posts a single Rendered Review link on each PR that changes Markdown.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><div class="fi"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 1.5l1.9 4 4.3.5-3.2 3 .9 4.3L8 11.2l-3.9 2.1.9-4.3-3.2-3 4.3-.5z"/></svg></div><h3>Open source</h3><p>AGPL-3.0-only. The code is on GitHub, and issues and pull requests are welcome.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <Pricing />

  <section id="docs" aria-labelledby="docs-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><div class="kicker">Docs</div><h2 id="docs-h">Start with the part you need</h2></div>
      <div class="docs">
        <a class="doc-card" href="/docs/deploy-cloudflare/"><h3><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7"></path></svg>Self-hosting</h3><p>Run your own instance on Cloudflare Workers, with the steps for sign-in and a custom domain.</p><span>Deploy it</span></a>
        <a class="doc-card" href="/docs/annotation-format/"><h3><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4L1.5 8 5 12M11 4l3.5 4-3.5 4"></path></svg>Annotation format</h3><p>How comments record their anchor in GitHub, and how they fall back.</p><span>Read the spec</span></a>
        <a class="doc-card" href="/docs/observability/"><h3><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"></circle><path d="M8 4.5V8l2.5 1.5"></path></svg>Observability</h3><p>What the server logs, and what it never logs.</p><span>See the events</span></a>
        <a class="doc-card" href="/docs/privacy-external-resources/"><h3><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 3.5h11v7h-6l-3 2.5v-2.5h-2z"></path></svg>External resources</h3><p>Why images from other servers never load without you asking.</p><span>Read about privacy</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap cta-band">
    <h2>Try it on a pull request you're reviewing</h2>
    <p>Public repositories are free and need no setup.</p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <Ext class="btn btn-primary" href={APP_URL}>Open a pull request</Ext>
      <a class="btn" href="#pricing">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
